**Theorem 4.3 (mode/frontier/general-prefix completeness).** For every
$h\in\mathcal C_{\mathrm{gc}}$, Definition 4.2 terminates on its basic
selected data and returns exactly $h$, its consumed input and $W(h)$.
It needs no later current payload and no completed endpoint descriptor.
Every source and mode/header/length/payload interior cut, all partial
bank/copy/return cuts and all earlier conversion rows satisfy the theorem.

Proof. The actual acquired seed and fixed public/code words give the
true original canonical supply, with the original site partition. This
is ARC's seed conversion, not an assumption that the changing current
source equals its initial value. Basic memory includes this seed and
the actual meter, hence the true $n$.

Induct on the simulated row ordinal $i\le n$. The initial state is the
same irreducible entrance. At a non-IN, equal prestates give the same
local guard, operation, finite effect, event and receipt by GCA's literal
Step correspondence. At a fixed canonical IN its supplied bit is the
actual one at that site. At a variable IN, $j=i$ and $d,w$ are therefore
the actual matching location and write ordinal. If $w\le n$, the write
has occurred and its bit remains at $d$. If $w>n$, IN has occurred but
not its matching WR; Lemma 4.1 forbids another input or a latch overwrite
before the endpoint, so family4's occupied record is exactly this bit.
Either branch supplies the actual bit. Thus the next complete state,
history event and receipt agree. Induction stops at the exact endpoint.

For a source preallocation the $w\le n$ test is indispensable: cells
allocated and initialized before their IN are not consulted as wire
data before their matching WR. For mode, the bit is consulted once from
the pending record or once from70; it cannot be lost between IN and WR
or counted twice after WR. EX alone adds no consumed input. A separate
length RD cannot overwrite a pending data latch. These statements also
cover an endpoint before/after MR, half-built counters and missing final
descriptors; no endpoint stage guess is required.

The proof interprets earlier converter code one native row at a time.
It does not call the result of a represented historical decoder. Each
Step and lookup is finite word work, and the outer countdown decreases
exactly once per row. Hence the procedure terminates even at a finite
cut of a flight whose future completion is not supplied. The role fold
then classifies constructed spans of the derived actual history. It
was not an input to this induction. ∎

